## Phase 1 — Constitution

```
/speckit.constitution Create the governing principles for WorkplaceIQ, a read-only
stock plan analytics web UI.

NON-NEGOTIABLE PRINCIPLES:

1. READ-ONLY BY CONSTRUCTION. The UI issues no mutating HTTP requests. No forms that
   submit, no elections, no transactions. Any requirement implying a write is a
   specification defect to be raised, not implemented.

2. NO CLIENT-SIDE FINANCIAL LOGIC. All aggregation, currency conversion, vesting
   calculation and rounding happen upstream in the Spring Batch layer. The UI formats
   values for display and never computes, sums or derives a financial figure.

3. DESIGN TOKENS ONLY. No literal hex colours, px spacing, font sizes, radii or
   shadow values in component code. Every visual value resolves to a token name from
   design/tokens.json. A literal visual value in a component is a defect.

4. FIGMA IS AUTHORITATIVE for layout and visual design, referenced by node ID from
   design/figma-sources.md. Where code and Figma disagree, Figma wins; any accepted
   deviation is recorded in the feature's design-context.md.

5. FOUR STATES MANDATORY. Every data-bound component implements loading, empty, error
   and stale/as-of states. A component with only a success path is incomplete.

6. COMPONENT REUSE. Screens are composed from the shared library described in
   design/design-system-rules.md. A new primitive requires documented justification.

7. CONTRACT-FIRST DATA ACCESS. The UI consumes the versioned OpenAPI contract at
   contracts/openapi.yaml. Client types are generated, never hand-written. The UI
   holds no knowledge of Snowflake schemas, table names or batch scheduling.

8. ACCESSIBILITY WCAG 2.2 AA. Every figure is announced with its unit, currency and
   as-of date. Colour is never the sole carrier of meaning in charts.

9. DATA HONESTY. The as-of timestamp is always visible on any screen showing figures.
   Stale or partial data is labelled as such rather than silently rendered.
```

Principles 3 and 5 are what actually buy you visual fidelity later. Principle 2 and 7 keep the
Snowflake / Spring Batch boundary from leaking into the UI.

Review the generated `.specify/memory/constitution.md` and edit by hand where it softened your
wording. Constitution text is loaded by `/speckit.plan` and `/speckit.analyze` on every feature,
so it is worth being pedantic about.

