## Phase 2 — Feature slicing

One feature = one `/speckit.specify` = one branch = one `specs/NNN-*/` folder. Never one
giant "build the UI" spec.

| # | Feature | Contains |
|---|---|---|
| 001 | `app-shell` | Layout, nav, header, token wiring, API client, global loading/error/empty patterns, shared KPI tile and data table |
| 002 | `portfolio-overview` | The dashboard screen |
| 003 | `grant-detail` | Per-grant drill-down |
| 004 | `vesting-schedule` | Timeline / schedule view |
| 005 | `tax-and-proceeds` | Analytics screens |

**Do 001 completely first.** Every later screen then composes real components instead of
inventing near-duplicates. This one decision removes most of the visual drift people report.

---

## Phase 3 — `/speckit.specify`

### What goes in, what stays out

| In `spec.md` | NOT in `spec.md` |
|---|---|
| Which screens exist and what they communicate | Colours, spacing, font sizes, px dimensions |
| Business meaning of each figure | Component names, framework, libraries |
| Filters, drill-downs, navigation | API endpoint paths, field names |
| Empty / loading / error / stale behaviour | Snowflake tables, batch schedule |
| Who sees what (participant vs admin) | Chart library choices |
| Figma frame **references** by node ID | Figma frame **contents** |
| Measurable success criteria | |

The spec command generates technology-agnostic success criteria verifiable without
implementation details, and will fill unspecified details with reasonable defaults recorded in
an Assumptions section. For a financial UI you want questions, not defaults — hence the last
line of the prompt below.

### Example — feature 002

```
/speckit.specify Portfolio Overview screen for WorkplaceIQ, a read-only stock plan
analytics application used by employees to view their equity awards.

DESIGN SOURCE — authoritative, reference only:
- Figma frame "Portfolio Overview / Desktop", node 1204:5567
- State variants: Empty 1204:5612, Loading 1204:5640, Error 1204:5668
- Extracted inventory: design/screen-inventory.md, section "Portfolio Overview"
- Screenshots: design/screens/portfolio-overview*.png
Read the Figma node via the Figma MCP server for context. Reference frames by name and
node ID only. Do NOT record colours, spacing, typography or pixel values in this spec —
those belong in the implementation plan.

USERS: employees holding equity awards; plan administrators viewing an employee in
read-only support mode.

WHAT THE SCREEN MUST COMMUNICATE:
- total portfolio value, broken down by award type
- vested vs unvested position
- upcoming vesting events across a user-selected horizon (3/6/12 months)
- exercisable quantity and awards expiring soon
- an unmissable as-of date for every figure shown

SCOPE CONSTRAINTS:
- DISPLAY ONLY. No transactions, exercises, elections, edits or persisted preferences.
  Filters and drill-down navigation are the only interactions. If the design appears to
  imply an action, raise it as [NEEDS CLARIFICATION] instead of specifying it.
- Data comes from an existing REST API populated by an upstream batch process. Treat the
  API as an external dependency. Do not specify warehouse, batch or API internals.

REQUIRED COVERAGE — write explicit requirements and acceptance scenarios for:
- empty: no awards at all; awards exist but none in the selected horizon
- loading, and behaviour when a response is slow
- error: API down; partial data; one widget fails while others succeed
- staleness: figures reflect the last completed batch run and must be labelled as such
- multi-currency display and which currency totals are expressed in
- zero, negative and very large values; awards missing optional attributes
- what an administrator in support mode may and may not see

KEY ENTITIES — business meaning only, no field names or types: grant, award type,
vesting tranche, vested quantity, unvested quantity, exercisable quantity, strike price,
current fair market value, expiration date.

SUCCESS CRITERIA — measurable and technology-agnostic. Include time to first meaningful
figure, correctness (every displayed figure traces to exactly one API field with no
client-side recomputation), and comprehension (a participant can state their vested value
and next vesting date without scrolling).

Mark anything my description or the design does not settle as [NEEDS CLARIFICATION].
Do not fill gaps with reasonable defaults.
```

**Produces:** branch `002-portfolio-overview`, `specs/002-portfolio-overview/spec.md`,
`checklists/requirements.md`, and updates `.specify/feature.json` so later commands know
which feature is active.

**Review before moving on.** Reject the spec and re-run if you see: hex codes or px values,
any framework name, any API path, or an Assumptions entry that silently answers a question
you wanted asked.

