## Phase 5 — `/speckit.plan` + the `design-context.md` file

This is the step Spec Kit leaves open — there is no built-in `/design` command, and the
maintainers' own discussion on where design guidance belongs is still unresolved. You close
the gap by explicitly asking `/speckit.plan` to produce a design-context artifact.

```
/speckit.plan Angular 18, standalone components, signals for state, SCSS with CSS custom
properties bound to design tokens.
[substitute your real stack]

DESIGN IMPLEMENTATION — produce specs/002-portfolio-overview/design-context.md:
- Use the Figma MCP server. Required order: get_metadata for the node map, then
  get_design_context for node 1204:5567 and each state variant, then get_screenshot for
  visual reference. Re-fetch narrower nodes if a response truncates.
- The MCP returns a React + Tailwind–shaped representation. That is design context, NOT
  our code style. Translate it to our stack and conventions.
- Follow design/design-system-rules.md for component and token mapping.
- For every component on the screen record: Figma component name and node ID; the TOKEN
  NAME (from design/tokens.json) for each colour, spacing, typography, radius and
  elevation value; auto-layout direction and gap; responsive behaviour at our breakpoints;
  and the mapping to an existing library component, or NEW if none exists.
- Never emit a raw hex or px value. If a Figma value has no matching token, list it under
  "## Token gaps" for the design team rather than hard-coding it.
- Map each of the four required states to its Figma variant node.

DATA ACCESS:
- Consume contracts/openapi.yaml. Generate the typed client; no hand-written DTOs.
- In data-model.md produce a table: UI element -> API response field -> formatting rule.
  Every displayed figure maps 1:1 to one field. No derived or recomputed values.
- Define caching, retry and staleness policy given data changes only once per batch cycle.
```

**Result — `specs/002-portfolio-overview/design-context.md` (excerpt):**

